--------------------------------------------------------------
BUG CONFIRMED: SHA256_DIGEST reads back as all-zero in BOTH scenarios, even though
the core's internal digest_reg holds a real, nonzero computed digest. The DIGEST.hwclr
polarity bug (zeroize_reg2 = Z | ~D instead of Z | D) permanently hardware-clears the
software-visible register whenever debug is locked (D=0, the normal/production case),
while a debug session (D=1) separately holds the whole core in reset via the still-
correct zeroize_reg. Net result: the digest read-back path is completely non-functional
in every reachable state -- a permanent denial-of-service of SHA256_DIGEST readback.
